findings.body:
The guard at `fetcher.py:397` changed from `full_name not in deployment_names` to `dep.name not in deployment_names`. For a short filter such as `--deployment production`, `dep.name` equals the filter value, so the whole block is skipped. `short_name_matches` then stays empty, and the "Short deployment name ... matched N deployments" warning never fires.

I ran `tests/_sdk/test_fetcher.py` at the head commit: `test_fetch_sdk_data_ambiguous_short_name_warning` fails (1 failed, 33 passed). Full `flow/deployment` filters still work because the later loop does the exact match, so the regression is limited to short names. The original `full_name not in deployment_names` check was correct, so the simplest fix is to revert this line.

::diff{file="src/prefect/_sdk/fetcher.py" lines="395-400"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The PR description and title never mention this change, and the test shows it was not run against the suite.

The async example in the guide awaits `future.result()`. `PrefectFlowRunFuture.result` is a plain `def` in `src/prefect/futures.py` (around line 410, inside the class that starts at line 340). `await` on its return value would raise `TypeError` once the flow finishes, so readers who copy the example will hit the error.

::code{file="docs/v3/advanced/generate-custom-sdk.mdx" lines="127-137"}

The fix is to drop the `await` on `result()`. If the example should stay non-blocking, `PrefectFlowRunFuture.wait_async()` (around line 373 of `futures.py`) is the awaitable option, and it has to be followed by a sync read.

::callout{type="info"}
The sync example on line 136 is fine.

`logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)` sits at line 20, between the top-level `import prefect` and the `from prefect._sdk.models import (...)` block. Ruff is configured with `extend-select = ["I"]` in `pyproject.toml`, and E402 is only exempted for `__init__.py`. Running `ruff check src/prefect/_sdk/fetcher.py` reports four errors: E402 on the imports after the logger, and an isort (I001) error.

::diff{file="src/prefect/_sdk/fetcher.py" lines="17-24"}

Move the logger below the import block, which is where the rest of the codebase puts it.

The new `v3/api-ref/cli/sdk` entry sits in the CLI group in alphabetical order, between `profiles` and `server`. The `Deployments` group contains the moved `form-building` page and the new guide. The CLI reference page uses the same conventions as the other CLI pages: a `title: " "` header, `\$`-escaped examples, `<ResponseField>` options, and a `(beta)` marker.

::callout{type="info"}
The flags (`--output`, `--flow`, `--deployment`, and their short aliases) match `src/prefect/cli/sdk.py`.
